WEBVTT

00:00:00.100 --> 00:00:10.925
In September 2019, the Quebec Superior Court ruled in Truchon versus Attorney General that the 'reasonably foreseeable natural death' requirement was unconstitutional.

00:00:10.875 --> 00:00:18.850
The federal government chose not to appeal the decision, creating a precedent for expanding access beyond terminal illnesses.
